CVA6ConfigDcacheByteSize = 2048 Signal Flow Tree
================================================

1. CONFIGURATION PHASE (cv32a6_imac_sv32_config_pkg.sv)
   └── localparam CVA6ConfigDcacheByteSize = 2048;
       └── cva6_cfg.'{ DcacheByteSize: unsigned'(CVA6ConfigDcacheByteSize) }

2. BUILD/DERIVATION PHASE (build_config_pkg.sv)
   └── CVA6Cfg.DcacheByteSize = 2048
       ├── DCACHE_INDEX_WIDTH calculation:
       │   └── $clog2(CVA6Cfg.DcacheByteSize / CVA6Cfg.DcacheSetAssoc)
       │       └── $clog2(2048 / 128) = $clog2(16) = 4
       │       └── BUT: Forced to 0 for FA cache (line 27)
       │
       └── DCACHE_NUM_WORDS calculation:
           └── (DCACHE_INDEX_WIDTH == 0) ? 1 : 2 ** (DCACHE_INDEX_WIDTH - DCACHE_OFFSET_WIDTH)
               └── Since INDEX_WIDTH = 0: NUM_WORDS = 1

3. MODULE INSTANTIATION PHASE
   └── std_cache_subsystem (core/cache_subsystem/std_cache_subsystem.sv)
       └── wt_cln_dcache_ctrler (core/cache_subsystem/wt_cln_dcache_ctrl.sv)
           └── wt_cln_dcache_mem (core/cache_subsystem/wt_cln_dcache_mem.sv)
               └── parameter DCACHE_CL_IDX_WIDTH = CONFIG.DCACHE_INDEX_WIDTH = 0

4. SIGNAL WIDTH IMPACT
   └── DCACHE_CL_IDX_WIDTH = 0
       ├── rd_idx_i [DCACHE_CL_IDX_WIDTH-1:0] → [0:0] (1-bit signal)
       ├── wr_cl_idx_i [DCACHE_CL_IDX_WIDTH-1:0] → [0:0] (1-bit signal)
       └── cl_index [DCACHE_CL_IDX_WIDTH-1:0] → [0:0] (1-bit signal)

5. MEMORY ORGANIZATION IMPACT
   └── SRAM Instantiation (wt_cln_dcache_mem.sv:89-103)
       └── for (genvar i = 0; i < DCACHE_SET_ASSOC; i++)
           └── sram #(.NUM_WORDS(DCACHE_NUM_WORDS))
               └── NUM_WORDS = 1 (single entry per way)
               └── 128 SRAM instances (one per way)
               └── Each SRAM has depth = 1 (fully associative)

6. FUNCTIONAL IMPACT
   └── Address Decoding:
       ├── All accesses use index 0 (single set)
       ├── Tag comparison happens across all 128 ways simultaneously
       └── Arbiter optimization:
           └── rd_wr_address_conflict = (DCACHE_CL_IDX_WIDTH == 0) ? 1'b0 : 1'b1
               └── In FA mode: Never block reads (no index conflicts possible)

KEY RELATIONSHIPS:
- DcacheByteSize (2048) determines total cache capacity
- With DcacheSetAssoc = 128, each way holds 16 bytes (one cache line)
- FA configuration: INDEX_WIDTH = 0 → NUM_WORDS = 1 → All ways in single set
- Performance impact: All 128 ways must be checked on every access